# Angular Template Conventions

## Accessibility

- Never use `<div (click)="...">` for interactive elements. Use `<button>` or `<a>` instead.
- Buttons must have `type="button"` unless they submit a form.
- When converting a `<div>` to `<button>`, add reset styles: `border: none; background: none; font: inherit; text-align: left; width: 100%;`.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<div class="card" (click)="openItem(item)">...</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<button class="card" (click)="openItem(item)" type="button">...</button>
```

## CSS / Layout

- When using flex layouts with text truncation (`text-overflow: ellipsis`), the text container must have `flex: 1` and `min-width: 0`.
